bucklespring-x11, the tray icon and the preferences window
==========================================================

The icon buckle puts in the system tray is a StatusNotifierItem. KDE Plasma
shows those natively. GNOME Shell does not, and needs an extension:

  # apt-get install gnome-shell-extension-appindicator
  $ gnome-extensions enable ubuntu-appindicators@ubuntu.com

The UUID is Ubuntu's, the extension having come from there. A running
gnome-shell does not notice an extension installed underneath it, and a
Wayland session cannot restart gnome-shell, so if that second command answers
"Extension ... does not exist", log out and back in and run it again.

If there's nothing to hold the icon, there is simply no icon. This is
mentioned with --verbose turned on. You can still get the configuration menu
with

  $ buckle-x11 --preferences

which tell the running buckle-x11 to pop it up. The desktop file has that as
an action, so a right click on the launcher offers "Bucklespring preferences".
SIGUSR1 does the same, for a keyboard shortcut.

 -- Barak A. Pearlmutter <bap@debian.org>, Fri, 30 Oct 2026 11:19:43 +0000
